but W7 gone, W5 only 1 left.  \nDiscarding W6 is even worse because W7 is gone and W3 only 1 left.  \n\nSo discard W4 to aim for a ready hand with W6 pair wait, and it also avoids discarding a middle tile (W5) that could be useful for chows in future draws.  \n\n**Answer:** Play W4"}
